# Getting Started

This guide covers cloning the repo, setting up the software environment on a Raspberry Pi, and running the board reader for the first time.

---

## Prerequisites

- Raspberry Pi 4 (2 GB RAM or more recommended)
- Raspberry Pi OS (Bookworm or later)
- Python 3.11+
- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)
- Git

---

## Software Setup

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/steve-birch/michess.git
cd michess
```

### 2. Run the current prototype

The `software/` package (`board_reader`, `chess_engine`, `led_controller`) isn't implemented yet - see [Project Status](index.md#project-status). Each harness under `development/` is an independent [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) project with its own `pyproject.toml`, virtual environment, and lockfile, so there's no repo-wide install step.

To run the NFC reader prototype:

```bash
cd development/nfc-matrix-tester
uv run nfc-matrix-tester
```

`uv run` creates the virtual environment and installs dependencies automatically on first use.

---

## Hardware Setup

Before running the software you'll need the physical board assembled and wired. See the [Hardware](hardware.md) page for:

- Component list and sourcing
- Multiplexer topology
- PCB and antenna assembly

---

## Repository Layout

```
michess/
├── hardware/               # Schematics, PCB layouts, BOM, antenna designs
├── firmware/                # Low-level microcontroller code (if applicable)
├── software/
│   ├── board_reader/       # NFC matrix scanning
│   ├── chess_engine/       # Stockfish/UCI integration
│   └── led_controller/     # LED matrix control
├── development/            # Throwaway hardware/learning test harnesses
├── docs/
└── tests/
```

---

